yunohost (12.1.41.43) stable; urgency=low

  * nostrhost: source extraction preserves tar/zip member modes.
    - SourceProvider._extract wrote every file with write_bytes(), dropping
      the archive's executable bits, so packaged binaries (e.g.
      opencode-web_nh) landed mode 0644 and their systemd units failed with
      EACCES under ProtectSystem=strict (the runtime chmod in run.sh cannot
      write to a read-only mount).
    - tar members now restore S_IMODE(member.mode); zip members restore the
      mode from external_attr when the archive records one.

 -- NostrHost <noreply@nostrhost.org>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0000 

yunohost (12.1.41.42) stable; urgency=low

  * nostrhost: portal settings transition to /etc/nostrhost (clean cut).
    - the portal apps/tiles projection is now regenerated by the native
      permission path: nostrhost.permissions.write_portal_projection writes
      /etc/nostrhost/portal/<domain>.json from the same user_permission_list
      the Caddy authd projection reads, so the portal SPA stops rendering zero
      tiles (the legacy /etc/yunohost/portal writer was only ever invoked by
      app_ssowatconf, which native installs never call).
    - write_permissions_projection refreshes the portal projection on every
      permission change (including when the authd map is unchanged), so tile
      visibility (show_tile/labels/urls) never goes stale.
    - PermissionProvider reconciles an existing permission by applying the URL
      before show_tile, because user_permission_update() silently downgrades
      show_tile=True to False when the permission has no URL yet.
    - portal_settings.py and the domain config panel read/write the native
      dir; the retired /etc/yunohost/portal path is gone.

 -- NostrHost <noreply@nostrhost.org>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:15:00 +0000 

yunohost (12.1.41.41) stable; urgency=low

  * nostrhost: post-install config panel for native package.toml apps.
    - native [settings] now generates a YunoHost-compatible config_panel.toml
      + scripts/config (legacy app registry), so app.config.read/set, the
      webadmin and the ConfigPanel machinery work on the same typed values the
      engine persists.
    - the config script validates/coerces against the declared field types,
      persists to the native settings state, re-renders the app's managed
      config templates with the new settings context, and reloads the app's
      service (native units are not in YunoHost's service registry, so the
      panel declares no services and the apply script handles the restart).
    - native manifest.json declares packaging_format 2 so the legacy manifest
      loader skips the v1->v2 conversion (which assumed an `arguments` table
      and crashed on the minimal native manifest).

 -- NostrHost <noreply@nostrhost.org>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:20:00 +0000 

yunohost (12.1.41.40) stable; urgency=low

  * nostrhost: operation executor + catalogue publish fixes.
    - catalog.publish passes --relay before the publish subcommand (Go
      flag.Parse stops at the first non-flag token), so publishes no longer
      fail with "publish requires --relay URL".
    - require websockets>=14.2: the 13.x sync client races receive_eof() in
      close_socket() without the protocol mutex, crashing the operationsd
      recv_events thread with AssertionError when a relay connection drops
      abruptly.
    - add kind-2205 (execution.progress) to the relay allowlist so progress
      publishes are acknowledged (allowlist mode silently drops disallowed
      kinds, stalling every op on the unacknowledged publish).

 -- NostrHost <noreply@nostrhost.org>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:03:00 +0000 

yunohost (12.1.41.39) stable; urgency=low

  * nostrhost: native API contract fixes for the admin console.
    - service.status accepts a names list (route now passes it through) so the
      Service Control screen works.
    - identity dicts use the Identity dataclass's 'username' field (not the
      removed 'ynh_username').
    - identity/list and identity/resolve wrap their lists in an object
      ({identities: [...]}) because Bottle's json plugin cannot serialise a
      top-level list.
    - responses are sanitised (datetimes -> ISO strings, sets -> sorted lists)
      so service.status's last_state_change serialises.
    - add /package/agent/{status,init,enable,disable} routes (the admin
      Agent screen needs them).
    - catalog/list wraps the bare CLI list in {entries: [...]}.

